{"book":24,"chapter":17,"context":{"chapter":17,"title":"Two Trees and a Deceitful Heart","summary":"The one who trusts in people is like a desert shrub, while the one who trusts the Lord is like a tree by water. God searches the deceitful heart, Jeremiah prays for healing, and the people are called to keep the Sabbath.","background":"'The horns of your altars' (v. 1) were the raised corners of an altar, touched with blood to make atonement (Leviticus 4:7); here sin is carved into them instead. Verses 5–8 closely resemble Psalm 1. Carrying goods through Jerusalem's gates on the Sabbath (vv. 19–27) stayed a problem; Nehemiah later shut the gates to stop it (Nehemiah 13:15-22).","customs":[{"term":"As the partridge sitteth on eggs","verses":"17:11","note":"Probably reflects an old belief that the partridge hatched eggs it did not lay, and the brood then left it. Wealth gained unjustly deserts its owner the same way."}],"watchFor":["Two contrasting pictures: shrub and tree (vv. 5–8).","'The heart is deceitful above all things' (v. 9), and God's answer (v. 10).","'Heal me, O Lord, and I shall be healed' (v. 14)."],"connections":["Psalms 1:1-3","Leviticus 4:7","Nehemiah 13:15-22","Matthew 15:19"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["חַטַּאת","chatat","H2403","HNcfsc","[the] sin of"],["יְהוּדָה","yehudah","H3063","HNpl","Judah"],["כְּתוּבָה","ketuvah","H3789","HVqsfsa","[is] inscribed"],["בְּעֵט","be'et","H5842","HR/Ncmsc","with a stylus of"],["בַּרְזֶל","barzel","H1270","HNcmsa","iron"],["בְּצִפֹּרֶן","betziporen","H6856","HR/Ncmsc","with a point of"],["שָׁמִיר","shamir","H8068","HNcmsa","flint"],["חֲרוּשָׁה","charushah","H2790","HVqsfsa","[is] engraved"],["עַל","'al-","H5921","HR","on"],["לוּחַ","luach","H3871","HNcmsc","[the] tablet of"],["לִבָּם","libam","H3820","HNcmsc/Sp3mp","heart their"],["וּלְקַרְנוֹת","ulekarnot","H7161","HC/R/Ncfpc","and to [the] horns of"],["מִזְבְּחוֹתֵיכֶם","mizbechoteikhem","H4196","HNcfpc/Sp2mp","altars your"]],"x":[[20003003,20003003,11],[47003003,4700